# Implementation Plan: Unattended Orchestration Control-Plane MCP Server

Build a dedicated Model Context Protocol (MCP) server (`unattended-orchestration-mcp`) to serve as a structured control plane and observability interface for autonomous unattended runs. This server bridges interactive AI agents (Antigravity/Gemini CLI, Claude Code, Grok, CodeWhale) with the underlying detached runner engine, enforcing strict 3-level subagent hierarchy boundaries and exposing real-time session and subagent progress through standard MCP tools and resources.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Runtime Stack & Transport Choice**:
> We propose implementing the server in **Python** using the official `mcp` SDK (`uv run --with mcp ...`), matching `trust_worktree.py` and Serena/Graphify. It will operate over standard **`stdio`** for direct client configuration (`.mcp.json` and Antigravity's global `mcp_config.json`), delegating detached execution loops to background supervisor tasks to avoid the stdio process-termination trap.

> [!WARNING]
> **Subagent Tool Boundary**:
> When an orchestrator spawns a subagent, the MCP server must restrict tool access:
> - **Level 1 (Main Orchestrator)**: Full access to all orchestration tools (`spawn_session`, `resume_session`, `stop_session`, `archive_session`) and resources.
> - **Level 2 (Phase Orchestrator)**: Restricted to spawning Level 3 tasks within its assigned phase.
> - **Level 3 (Task Workers / Leaves)**: **Zero orchestration tools**; read-only access to status resources (`handoff://sessions`), preventing recursive delegation cascades.

